Description: serial-to-network bridge with a web UI
 ser2netweb shares local serial ports over the network as raw TCP, telnet,
 RFC 2217 or UDP, is a Modbus RTU/TCP gateway and publishes serial data and
 Modbus points to MQTT and Sparkplug B. Everything is set up in a web UI
 with accounts, roles, two-factor sign-in, an audit log, a REST API and a
 cluster view of several machines; a web console shows a port's traffic
 live.
 .
 The package installs a hardened systemd unit, which runs it as the system
 account ser2netweb with its data in /var/lib/ser2netweb; it is not enabled
 by default. The recommended packages add MQTT publishing, LDAP and OpenID
 Connect sign-in and self-signed TLS certificates.
 .
 ser2netweb is an independent project, not related to the ser2net daemon
 (package ser2net), whose configuration files it can import; the two
 install side by side.
